From 2f9ab306795e48feb1f19f628de612d7426fdfdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 22:04:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add run_all.sh, cache the scoring, and write up the sweep
 and the basis check

- deconv_comparison/run_all.sh reproduces the whole package from an empty
  data/, with NREP and NPROC overridable.
- score.py caches its per-voxel measurements in data/score_<tag>.npz. Peak
  extraction over 40,000 voxels times four methods is a couple of minutes and
  both the tables and the figure want it.
- REPORT sections 4, 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10: the convention checks, the
  lambda_nonneg sweep, the exact-response control, the limits, how to
  reproduce, and what to do next. Section 5 waits on the remaining arms.

Two measured findings recorded there:

SMI's SH basis differs from MRtrix's by (-1)^m at the default CS_phase = 1,
which for even l is exactly a reflection through z = 0. A sharp fODF along
[0.301 -0.501 0.812] written out at CS_phase = 1 and read in MRtrix's basis
comes back at [0.327 -0.499 -0.803], 72.32 degrees off; at CS_phase = 0 it
comes back 1.65 degrees off, which is the Lmax 6 band limit of the test fODF
itself. This is the open item in "README for Claude" section 8 item 4.

lambda_nonneg = 10, the shipped default, is not on the Pareto front: it has the
worst angular correlation of the four constrained settings at every condition
and resolves 0.0% of 45 degree crossings, where lambda_nonneg = 1 resolves
63.5% and has the best ACC everywhere. The default was NOT changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GptEuETZEw1QVJAj7e9vag
